  "narrative": {
    "text": "The TOWS matrix: strengths and weaknesses across the top, opportunities and threats down the side, each cell naming the strategy that pairing implies. SO — achieve opportunities that greatly match the organization's strengths. WO — overcome weaknesses to attain opportunities. ST — use strengths to reduce vulnerability to threats. WT — prevent weaknesses to avoid making the organization more susceptible to threats. This is the step that turns the four lists into strategy.",
